  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-guard",
      "text": "One plugin, two surfaces. Static analysis only — never executes the target plugin.\n\n| Surface | Tool | Job |\n|---|---|---|\n| Gate | `plugin_audit` | Static audit before install |\n| Gate | `plugin_verify` | Hash + capability lock after install |\n| Clinic | `plugin_peers` | Local fingerprint peers; `query` searches GitHub `topic:dsh-plugin` |\n| Clinic | `plugin_detox` | Mechanical amputation, not an equivalent rewrite |"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-guard",
      "text": "`plugin_peers`: `path` stays local (profile bundles). `query` hits GitHub `topic:dsh-plugin` + the curated list; argo only if those are thin. Override with `remote`. Remote hits are `verdict=unknown` — audit before install."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:taxueseek/dsh-plugin-guard"
    },
    {
      "section": "restart dsh web",
      "text": "```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Scoring",
      "text": "Start at 100; P0 −40, P1 −12, P2 −3. Any P0 or score < 40 → `block`. Any P1 or score < 75 → `warn`.\n\nP0 is only auto-run + dangerous combo (`curl|bash`, secrets leaving the machine, eval of network content, install-script poison). `exec` inside a tool the model must click is P1."
    },
    {
      "section": "Not",
      "text": "- Not output redaction\n- Not general SAST\n- Does not prove a plugin is safe\n- Detox does not keep the original behavior"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
